# feature-map: every page and route handler under app/ belongs to a feature in docs/features/, and every
# surface, source glob and test anchor the map lists still resolves (docs/features/README.md).
feature-map --surface page 'app/**/page.tsx' --surface route 'app/**/route.ts'
# repo-rules runs the catalog's typescript pack: bugs that pass type checks, plus a new @ts-ignore,
# @ts-nocheck, bare eslint-disable or silenced React hooks rule (blocking) and an unchecked cast of
# outside data (advisory). It ratchets per rule and file, so what main already has never blocks.
repo-rules --pack typescript
# prose: an em dash, or an en dash used as an aside, on a Markdown line a pull request adds blocks (house
# style); a curly quote and the pull request description are advisory. Only added lines count, so the
# docs as they stand never block.
prose
